B = [
('Triumph Motorcycles','Europe','1950s-present','motorcycles','In the style of Triumph Motorcycles, British heritage with a lean, confident edge. Surfaces are solid enamel in cream, silver, deep green, racing red and blaze yellow, divided by crisp two-tone breaks and thin hand-painted gold pinstripes. Lettering is a flowing gold or white cursive signature with fine outlines, alongside a clean modern capital wordmark set in a shield badge with a union-flag quarter motif. Brushed and polished metal, black satin, ribbed rubber and rich brown leather provide contrast. Small enamel roundels, knurled textures and tidy rivets add craft. Proportions feel compact, tapered and understated, nostalgic yet sporty.'),
('Indian Motorcycle','North America','1930s-present','motorcycles','In the style of Indian Motorcycle, lavish American art deco craft. Deep lacquered cherry red meets ivory cream, black and gold, with long teardrop curves and hand-laid pinstripes along edges. Lettering is a bold, slanted, looping script in red with white outline, often paired with a small stacked capital word beneath. A proud profile emblem of a feathered headdress appears as a carved, enamelled or stitched mark. Surfaces mix mirror chrome, glossy candy paint, tan leather with brass studs, and glowing amber ornaments. Winged, swooping shapes, rounded oval cartouches and heritage patches give a rich, proud, polished character.'),
('Lambretta','Europe','1950s-present','scooters','In the style of Lambretta, Italian mod-era pop style built from clean geometry. Smooth enamel shapes in cream, white, red, sky blue and olive green, often split into two clean tones by a long horizontal break. Italian tricolour shield badges, concentric target roundels in blue, white and red, and black and white checkerboard bands repeat as signature graphics. Lettering is a heavy, rounded, slightly condensed script with a thick underline and drop outline, in white on black or silver on enamel. Brushed aluminium, chrome trim and flat matte panels look tidy and precise. Youthful, witty, minimal and sharply graphic, with retro ska energy.'),
('Kawasaki','East Asia','1970s-present','motorcycles','In the style of Kawasaki, loud, fast, race-ready graphic punch. Signature fluorescent lime green dominates, cut by black, white and occasional pale blue in sharp angular slashes, jagged shards, diagonal speed bands and torn-edge digital camouflage patterns. A bold angular wordmark in black or white, wide and italic with squared letters, and a stylised capital letter emblem in a sharp frame repeat across large sticker-like graphics. Numerals in thick racing type sit inside rounded plates. Surfaces are high-gloss, carbon-weave and matte black with tinted metallic highlights. Aggressive, athletic and unapologetically vivid.'),
('Honda Super Cub','East Asia','1950s-present','motorcycles','In the style of Honda Super Cub, cheerful Japanese everyday charm. Bright, simple solid colours in poppy red, cream white, deep navy and soft teal, with generous clean white borders and a single contrasting stripe panel. Lettering is a friendly, brush-like, rounded red script, slanted and bold, often set inside a soft oval outline or beside a black and white checkered border. A winged emblem in red, silver and white appears on round enamel badges with polished metal rims. Pressed, smooth, softly rounded surfaces with glossy paint, chrome edging and simple decal graphics feel warm, honest, practical and endearing.'),
('Moto Guzzi','Europe','1920s-present','motorcycles','In the style of Moto Guzzi, proud Italian craft in red, silver and black. A glossy elongated oval badge in rich red holds a spread-winged eagle in silver and gold above a bold capital wordmark with wide, even letter spacing. Round red and gold roundels, thin gold edge lines and tricolour stripes in green, white and red appear as recurring accents. Surfaces are deep lacquer, mirror-polished chrome, brushed alloy and warm tan leather. Shapes are smooth, generous, long and teardrop-like with calm, balanced curves. The mood is dignified, mechanical, sophisticated and confident, with wings as an ornamental motif for pattern work.'),
('Schwinn','North America','1930s-1970s','bicycles','In the style of Schwinn, American mid-century craft in candy enamel and bright metal. Elongated oval and shield-shaped badges in aluminium or chrome hold a bold stylised capital wordmark in tall condensed letters with a compass-like star at the centre, often on red, navy, green or yellow backgrounds. Colour blocking in cherry red, tropical turquoise, canary yellow, deep green and cream, with thin white or gold pinstripes and chunky outlined script. Gleaming chrome edging, rivet studs, glossy lacquer and enamel pin finishes. Balloon-round, streamlined, swooping forms with playful, sturdy, optimistic nostalgic character.'),
('Raleigh','Europe','1900s-present','bicycles','In the style of Raleigh, English heritage craft with an ornamental metal-badge tradition. A tall, sculpted crest in brass and enamel shows an elegant long-necked heron over a looping interlaced capital initial, in red, deep blue, cream and gold cloisonne colours. Lettering is a serif capital wordmark, framed in a pointed shield or heart-like outline with a fine engraved border. Deep gloss green, black, maroon and cream enamel is lined with hand-painted gold pinstripes. Polished brass, patinated copper, riveted tan leather and chrome details give a refined, tidy, old-world, countryside gentleman feel with fine hand-finished decorative attention.'),
('John Deere','North America','1900s-present','tractors','In the style of John Deere, rural American utility with a bold two-colour identity. A vivid leaf green paired with strong sunflower yellow, in flat solid blocks and clean contrasting edges. A leaping deer silhouette in yellow sits inside a rounded square or framed green panel with a thin yellow outline, beside a clean slab or sans wordmark in capital letters. Stitched patches, woven twill, heavy canvas, enamelled metal plaques and matte painted surfaces carry the mark. Simple, symmetrical, no-nonsense layout with sturdy proportions, practical, dependable, honest and recognisable at a glance.'),
('Greyhound','North America','1930s-1960s','buses','In the style of Greyhound, mid-century American speed graphics. A streamlined racing dog silhouette in long, low, stretched motion, in white or silver on deep cobalt blue, set inside a wide oval or rounded plate with thick border. Colour blocking in navy, royal blue, white, silver and a punchy orange or red, with a bold italic capital wordmark that leans forward. Surfaces recall glossy porcelain enamel, polished aluminium, stainless metal and pressed cut-out shapes with rivets. Smooth swept lines, ovals and speed streaks give a confident, optimistic, travel-poster look, simple, flat and highly legible.'),
]
